  <main id="main" class="max-w-[720px] mx-auto px-6 pt-12 pb-12 flex-1 w-full">
<%- include('../partials/legal-header.ejs', { heading: 'Accessibility' }) %>
    <div class="mt-10 font-serif text-[17px] leading-[1.8]">
      <p>I want this website to be usable by everyone. It is built to conform to the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 at level AA.</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-[20px] font-semibold mt-10">Status</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">As far as I can tell, all pages of paulwerner.net meet WCAG 2.1 AA. This is a self-assessment from 21 November 2026, not an external audit. It combined automated testing (axe-core, Lighthouse) with manual checks of keyboard navigation, heading structure, colour contrast and reduced-motion behaviour.</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-[20px] font-semibold mt-10">Known Limitations</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>The site has not been tested with users of assistive technology, and automated tools find only some barriers.</li>
        <li>Blog articles at blog.paulwerner.net can contain images, embedded media or code samples whose accessibility depends on the individual post. They are not covered by this statement.</li>
        <li>All content is in English only.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-[20px] font-semibold mt-10">Feedback</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">If you run into a barrier, write to <a href="mailto:contact@paulwerner.net" class="text-link hover:text-hover underline underline-offset-2">contact@paulwerner.net</a> with the page address and a short description. I will fix confirmed problems as soon as I can.</p>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-[20px] font-semibold mt-10">Legal Note</h2>
      <p class="mt-4">This statement is voluntary. To my understanding, the German Accessibility Strengthening Act (Barrierefreiheitsst&auml;rkungsgesetz &ndash; BFSG) does not apply to this website: it presents my freelance work and offers no products or services to consumers, and one-person businesses that provide services are exempt as micro-enterprises (Sec. 3 (3) BFSG).</p>

      <p class="mt-10 text-muted text-[15px]">Last updated: 2026-11-21</p>
    </div>
  </main>
